Outlined by the prime minister's office: The general budget revenues, set at 5,932.2 billion FCFA for the year 2026, include:

tax revenues estimated at 5,384.8 billion FCFA, mainly driven by tax revenues from the PRES for 703.6 billion FCFA;

non-tax and other revenues amount to 355.9 billion FCFA;

Drawdowns on grant-projects valued at 145.2 billion FCFA, down 54.8 billion FCFA compared to 2025;

budgetary donations amount to 46.3 billion FCFA.

Outlined by the prime minister's office. The general budget expenditures, budgeted at 7,177.2 billion FCFA for 2026, are broken down as follows:

interest and commissions on the public debt increased to 1,190.6 billion FCFA;

Projected personnel expenses of 1,532.8 billion FCFA;

expenditure on acquisitions of goods and services and current transfers set at 1,650 billion FCFA;

Capital expenditures from internal resources are projected at 1,448.9 billion FCFA;

Capital expenditures from external resources increased to 1,355.0 billion FCFA.

